## Objective

Close the next shared-Core reference gap identified in the capability map: compose the already-reviewed process-local single-use Gate with the already-reviewed filesystem durable claim primitive, without depending on Wallet Guard PR #93 and without changing historical `pom-rx/0.1` semantics.

Base at branch creation: trusted `main` `818718955c9e4136e9e55754a31be2f1c7b610f8` (PR #96 exact-merge-SHA assurance PASS).

## Scope

- add `core/gate/reference-durable-single-use-gate.mjs` as a composition boundary;
- create the durable store internally from an exact `rootDir` bootstrap rather than trusting a caller-supplied structural store;
- synchronously reserve the local wrapper before any await;
- acquire the durable capability tombstone before the inner Core Gate can observe binding or reach downstream;
- keep validation rejection fail-closed by leaving the durable claim `RESERVED` instead of fabricating a consumed terminal outcome;
- persist `CONSUMED_SUCCESS` / `CONSUMED_ERROR` only after downstream actually resolves/rejects, and do not return a successful result until the success terminal marker is durable;
- expose only `consume()` on the untrusted Gate handle; keep issuance and local/durable inspection test-only;
- capture the new composition boundary's reflection/WeakMap intrinsics at module initialization;
- add CI-wired tests for persisted success/error, external-store replay blocking before observer/downstream, cross-store race cardinality, post-claim binding rejection, local concurrency and bootstrap Proxy/accessor zero-side-effect rejection;
- document ordering, failure semantics, trust assumptions and deliberate non-claims in `core/gate/DURABLE-COMPOSITION.md`.

## Architecture / safety

This is common POM-RX Core work. It does not fork Wallet Guard behavior, does not widen strict-verifier/canonicalization/reference-data limits, and does not alter Witness, application policy or historical receipt semantics. Wallet Guard remains an application profile and is not imported here.

The composition remains reference-only. Production issuer/trusted-time/Witness trust service, network/distributed filesystem semantics, consensus, crash recovery, external execution/effect truth, simulation-to-forwarding binding and production readiness remain unproved.

No private key, seed, secret, funded wallet, network transaction, testnet/mainnet execution or meaningful funds are used.

## Merge gates

Do not merge until exact-head CI passes, release-owner SpecKit/falsification/security/code-quality/optimization/integration review passes on the exact head, and a distinct fresh independent skeptical/security review covers that exact head with no unresolved P0/P1/P2. The independent-review waiver remains limited to PR #60. Because PR #93 also touches `package.json`, this PR must be reconciled with the then-current trusted `main` before merge if #93 lands first.

After merge, mandatory exact-merge-SHA post-merge assurance is required before this composition is treated as trusted.

Retargets the existing one-shot Windows generation-barrier applicator to the live upstream `main` while preserving the reviewed patch and preimage authority.

The runner still:

- verifies the combined patch SHA-256;
- verifies every touched preimage blob is byte-identical to the reviewed implementation base;
- applies only the six generation-barrier source/test files;
- runs `py_compile` and the focused Windows generation/lock suites;
- commits and pushes only those exact paths.

The only behavioral change is removing the obsolete hard-coded upstream commit gate. Current upstream is accepted only when all reviewed preimage blobs remain exact, so unrelated main movement cannot silently alter the implementation.

Temporary fork control-plane change; it will be removed after the source branch is materialized.
